  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "sort-guidance",
      "scriptSha256": "c903a009e68d51d9ac54b988e7a6b255f494061a977b6ad1d9630e103012081a",
      "durationFrames": 592,
      "cues": [
        {
          "start": 0.405,
          "end": 3.085,
          "text": "Picture two issues in the same\nrepository."
        },
        {
          "start": 3.163,
          "end": 5.296,
          "text": "One is about zero quantities."
        },
        {
          "start": 5.374,
          "end": 7.95,
          "text": "Another asks for a clearer error\nmessage."
        },
        {
          "start": 8.002,
          "end": 10.835,
          "text": "The issue ID and expected behavior\nchange."
        },
        {
          "start": 11.451,
          "end": 15.458,
          "text": "The location of the test suite may stay\nthe same across both."
        },
        {
          "start": 15.51,
          "end": 19.256,
          "text": "Put recurring project conventions where\nthe agent can load them,"
        },
        {
          "start": 19.308,
          "end": 23.142,
          "text": "and keep the individual issue details in\nthe prompt you send for that task."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "prompt-template",
      "scriptSha256": "a498c7e80fd19ecba8df7a23001c46d6e333c05a08e8a21ceff5763698b85ef5",
      "durationFrames": 543,
      "cues": [
        {
          "start": 0.409,
          "end": 3.869,
          "text": "Open a Markdown template in the training\nrepository."
        },
        {
          "start": 3.947,
          "end": 8.259,
          "text": "Write a request that takes an issue and\nthe current source and tests as inputs."
        },
        {
          "start": 8.913,
          "end": 13.455,
          "text": "Ask for the proposed edit, the affected\nfiles, and a way to verify it."
        },
        {
          "start": 13.507,
          "end": 16.369,
          "text": "The template should end at a plan you\ncan review."
        },
        {
          "start": 16.473,
          "end": 20.886,
          "text": "On the approved Copilot setup, paste the\nfilled-in text into chat to run it."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "context-run",
      "scriptSha256": "177826cd46b62a28c82ebad6d7a72a8983eb8e401e572240649f9f5ca41e784b",
      "durationFrames": 622,
      "cues": [
        {
          "start": 0.453,
          "end": 4.225,
          "text": "Start Plan in the current branch and\nattach the issue, validator,"
        },
        {
          "start": 4.277,
          "end": 6.046,
          "text": "and matching test file."
        },
        {
          "start": 6.125,
          "end": 8.614,
          "text": "Paste the template with the issue\nreference filled in."
        },
        {
          "start": 9.236,
          "end": 13.477,
          "text": "The response should identify the\nexisting comparison and explain why a"
        },
        {
          "start": 13.529,
          "end": 15.715,
          "text": "zero test would expose it."
        },
        {
          "start": 15.793,
          "end": 18.401,
          "text": "Open the cited lines and check them\nyourself."
        },
        {
          "start": 19.05,
          "end": 23.655,
          "text": "If a file name is unfamiliar, confirm it\nin the workspace before accepting the"
        },
        {
          "start": 23.707,
          "end": 24.169,
          "text": "plan."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "instructions",
      "scriptSha256": "c14c16ee3f4a5d289cf99bbced7e150829130ab69c8f30368236384f0682c659",
      "durationFrames": 639,
      "cues": [
        {
          "start": 0.409,
          "end": 3.453,
          "text": "Open the repository root in VS Code."
        },
        {
          "start": 3.531,
          "end": 8.526,
          "text": "For this Copilot example, find or create\nthe project instructions file in the dot"
        },
        {
          "start": 8.579,
          "end": 9.546,
          "text": "GitHub folder."
        },
        {
          "start": 10.2,
          "end": 15.273,
          "text": "Add the convention that unit tests use\nthe existing unittest suite under tests."
        },
        {
          "start": 15.351,
          "end": 19.228,
          "text": "Keep the rule short and include a\nreliable reference for the verification"
        },
        {
          "start": 19.28,
          "end": 19.779,
          "text": "command."
        },
        {
          "start": 20.438,
          "end": 24.847,
          "text": "If instructions already exist, edit the\nexisting guidance with your team."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "discovery",
      "scriptSha256": "0ce9dec8c4dcf39897127c0dfe3471a06f8ddb130d9ac31708453d83bd09e90d",
      "durationFrames": 588,
      "cues": [
        {
          "start": 0.409,
          "end": 4.806,
          "text": "Open the agent customizations view and\nfind the instruction file."
        },
        {
          "start": 4.884,
          "end": 7.902,
          "text": "Then start a fresh chat in the same\nworkspace."
        },
        {
          "start": 7.98,
          "end": 11.278,
          "text": "Ask for a regression plan without\nrepeating the test convention."
        },
        {
          "start": 11.916,
          "end": 15.881,
          "text": "Where your client shows references,\nconfirm the file was included."
        },
        {
          "start": 15.959,
          "end": 19.003,
          "text": "Read the proposed test location and\nframework."
        },
        {
          "start": 19.107,
          "end": 22.707,
          "text": "File discovery and correct use give you\ntwo different things to check."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "roles",
      "scriptSha256": "65ccc201eeae87aae0a2c9cad9d4e7ed38c172d4167adccfd38e77c7a7fdae78",
      "durationFrames": 670,
      "cues": [
        {
          "start": 0.405,
          "end": 3.293,
          "text": "The prompt asks for a particular piece\nof work."
        },
        {
          "start": 3.345,
          "end": 7.326,
          "text": "The instruction file supplies reusable\nproject conventions."
        },
        {
          "start": 7.378,
          "end": 11.278,
          "text": "Required checks and actual tool\npermissions enforce separate boundaries."
        },
        {
          "start": 11.974,
          "end": 16.085,
          "text": "Some VS Code versions also offer\nrunnable prompt files,"
        },
        {
          "start": 16.137,
          "end": 19.077,
          "text": "with support depending on the selected\nharness."
        },
        {
          "start": 19.129,
          "end": 22.286,
          "text": "The Markdown template in this example is\nready to paste."
        },
        {
          "start": 22.956,
          "end": 26.41,
          "text": "In the next lesson, we’ll make a\nrecurring procedure into a skill."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "practice",
      "scriptSha256": "bd700943736a121cd232dad223811821c1b17c9ab6c31043a3317e09a7c16562",
      "durationFrames": 558,
      "cues": [
        {
          "start": 0.435,
          "end": 3.505,
          "text": "Use the template for a second synthetic\nissue."
        },
        {
          "start": 3.583,
          "end": 7.512,
          "text": "Swap the issue reference and attach the\ncurrent files for that task."
        },
        {
          "start": 7.59,
          "end": 11.675,
          "text": "Compare the two plans and find one part\nthat changed because the requirement"
        },
        {
          "start": 11.727,
          "end": 12.389,
          "text": "changed."
        },
        {
          "start": 13.048,
          "end": 16.092,
          "text": "Then find the test convention that\ncarried over."
        },
        {
          "start": 16.17,
          "end": 19.813,
          "text": "A teammate should be able to reproduce\nthat setup in a fresh session with the"
        },
        {
          "start": 19.891,
          "end": 21.276,
          "text": "same project files."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
